[Audio:start-up-tune:Start-up Tune]
Played by #R$A650 each time a new game is started.
The music data is at #R$B3C5.

#AUDIO0(start-up-tune.wav)(#INCLUDE(StartUpTune))

[Audio:robot-tune:Robot Tune]
Played by #R$A971 when the robot has come back up out of the pot of oil in the
game completed scene.
The music data is at #R$B3D7.

#AUDIO0(robot-tune.wav)(#INCLUDE(RobotTune))

[Audio:game-over-tune:Game Over Tune]
Played by #R$B761 when the game is over, until a key is pressed.
The music data is at #R$B3F7.

#AUDIO0(game-over-tune.wav)(#INCLUDE(GameOverTune))

[Audio:game-complete-tune:Game Complete Tune]
Played by #R$B8A9 when the player has completed the game.
The music data is at #R$B437.

#AUDIO0(game-complete-tune.wav)(#INCLUDE(GameCompleteTune))

[Audio:main-tune:Main Tune]
Played by #R$BA7E when the menu is first shown, until a key is pressed.
The music data is at #R$B451.

#AUDIO0(main-tune.wav)(#INCLUDE(MainTune))

[Audio:block-sound:Block Sound]
Not played by the game, as nothing calls #R$B5D4.
Four cycles of each of the eight pitches of #R$B5E6, one after the other.

#AUDIO0(block-sound.wav)(#INCLUDE(BlockSound))

[Audio:sparkles-sound:Sparkles Sound]
Played by #R$AF79 and #R$B3A4 for each stage of the sparkles.
The eight stages of the sparkles, one after the other.

#AUDIO0(sparkles-sound.wav)(#INCLUDE(SparklesSound))

[Audio:appearing-sound:Appearing Sound]
Played by #R$BC70 for each stage of the sparkles that show the player appearing.
The seven stages, one after the other.

#AUDIO0(appearing-sound.wav)(#INCLUDE(AppearingSound))

[Audio:bounce-sound:Bounce Sound]
Played by #R$AB61, #R$B06B and #R$B110 when a robot mouse bumps into something
and when a tool hits the robot.
Four short bursts of a tone.

#AUDIO0(bounce-sound.wav)(#INCLUDE(BounceSound))

[Audio:jump-sound:Jump Sound]
Played by #R$C23D when the player jumps.
A sweep of thirty-two single cycles.

#AUDIO0(jump-sound.wav)(#INCLUDE(JumpSound))

[Audio:falling-sound:Falling Sound]
Played by #R$A8F9, #R$A9C7, #R$AD13, #R$B06B, #R$B2B6, #R$B33F and #R$C296 while
an object falls or rises.
The pitch comes from the height of the object, so here the object falls
through sixteen heights, one after the other.

#AUDIO0(falling-sound.wav)(#INCLUDE(FallingSound))

[Audio:rising-sound:Rising Sound]
Played by #R$A971 while the robot goes down into the pot of oil and comes back
up in the game completed scene.
The pitch comes from the pixel y position of the robot, so here the robot
goes down and comes back up.

#AUDIO0(rising-sound.wav)(#INCLUDE(RisingSound))

[Audio:block-east-west-sound:Block East West Sound]
Played by #R$B224 while a block moves east or west.
The pitch comes from the X coordinate of the block, so here the block
moves through ten positions, one after the other.

#AUDIO0(block-east-west-sound.wav)(#INCLUDE(BlockEastWestSound))

[Audio:block-north-south-sound:Block North South Sound]
Played by #R$B21C while a block moves north or south.
The pitch comes from the Y coordinate of the block, so here the block
moves through ten positions, one after the other.

#AUDIO0(block-north-south-sound.wav)(#INCLUDE(BlockNorthSouthSound))

[Audio:moving-sound:Moving Sound]
Played by #R$B3BF when a valve, a sparkle, a block, an extra life or a retired
object moves.
The pitch comes from the three coordinates of the object, so here the
object rises through sixteen heights, one after the other.

#AUDIO0(moving-sound.wav)(#INCLUDE(MovingSound))

[Audio:transform-sound:Transform Sound]
Not played by the game, as nothing calls #R$B65F.
The pitch comes from the sprite number of an object, so here four sprite
numbers are used three times each.

#AUDIO0(transform-sound.wav)(#INCLUDE(TransformSound))

[Audio:explosion:Explosion]
Played by #R$AB61 and #R$AD54 when a tool hits the robot and when an object
lands.
Sixteen short bursts of a tone, with pitches from a random place in the ROM.
The game picks the place at random, so here it is fixed.

#AUDIO0(explosion.wav)(#INCLUDE(Explosion))

[Audio:beep-sound:Beep Sound]
Played by #R$ABF5, #R$BA7E, #R$BD6B and #R$BEE0 when the alarm changes colour,
when the player picks up or drops an object, gets an extra life or changes the
control method on the menu.
Sixteen cycles of a low tone.

#AUDIO0(beep-sound.wav)(#INCLUDE(BeepSound))

[Audio:pause-sound:Pause Sound]
Played by #R$CE22 when the game is paused and when it carries on again.
Twenty-four cycles of a high tone.

#AUDIO0(pause-sound.wav)(#INCLUDE(PauseSound))

[Audio:high-beep-sound:High Beep Sound]
Played by #R$AAA1 and #R$B267 when a clockwork mouse chooses a new direction and
when something lands on a conveyor.
Thirty-two cycles of a higher tone.

#AUDIO0(high-beep-sound.wav)(#INCLUDE(HighBeepSound))

[Audio:robot-moving-sound:Robot Moving Sound]
Played by #R$A9C7 and #R$AA89 while the remote control robot or the chasing dome
moves.
The length and pitch come from the frame counter, so here sixteen
frames are played, one after the other.

#AUDIO0(robot-moving-sound.wav)(#INCLUDE(RobotMovingSound))

[Audio:mouse-footstep-sound:Mouse Footstep Sound]
Played by #R$B055 as a robot mouse moves.
The pitch comes from the position, so here the mouse takes eight steps
along a line.

#AUDIO0(mouse-footstep-sound.wav)(#INCLUDE(MouseFootstepSound))

[Audio:footstep-sound:Footstep Sound]
Played by #R$C1E2 and #R$C25E as the player walks.
The pitch comes from the position of the player, so here the player takes
eight steps along a line.

#AUDIO0(footstep-sound.wav)(#INCLUDE(FootstepSound))
